WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
On the Home screen, click Open project… and choose the project of the tutorial The full processing: stars apart.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The project opens up to date: nothing is to be computed.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Click Post.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Before any gesture: the dark globules and the folds of the ring are flat, and the ring could be a little more vivid.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Click the combined layer: it holds two rows, Stars and Starless image.

6
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The stars are added over the starless image in Screen mode.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Click Stars: its sliders, Strength and Small stars, act on the stars only.

8
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Click Starless image: its filters apply to it only, before the stars are put back.

9
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Click Filter: the families are Stretch, Contrast, Color, Detail, Noise and Combine.

10
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Open Contrast.

11
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Choose Local contrast.

12
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Drag Strength to about 0.5, with Scale left at 40 px: the globules and the folds stand out.

13
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Click Filter again.

14
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Open Color.

15
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Choose Saturation.

16
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Drag Strength to about +20 %, all hues: the red and pink of the ring get more vivid.

17
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Click the eye of Saturation: the filter is switched off.

18
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Click the eye again: the filter is back, with its setting.

19
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.000
The same with Local contrast: the globules go flat when it is off.

20
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Click a filter: its settings are still there and can be changed.

21
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Drag Strength further, to see.

22
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Select Saturation.

23
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Click the trash button: the filter is deleted.

24
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Press Ctrl+Z: the filter is back, with its setting.

25
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Click Duplicate (Ctrl+J): the chosen filter is copied, here Local contrast.

26
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Click the trash button: the copy is deleted.

27
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Click the combined layer: Star blend mode reads Screen.

28
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Drag Opacity of Local contrast to about 55 %: the filter acts by half.

29
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Press Ctrl+Z: Opacity is back at 100 %.

30
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Press Ctrl+S: the layers and their filters are saved with the project.

31
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Open File, then click Close project.

32
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.000
The Home screen lists the project.

33
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Click the project to open it again.

34
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Click Post.

35
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:29.000
The filters are still there; a click on one opens its settings, still editable.
